1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,646
This tutorial closes periods and a fiscal
year in Miftah.

2
00:00:03,646 --> 00:00:06,199
Open Accounting and choose Year End
Closing.

3
00:00:06,199 --> 00:00:08,751
The period lock reads 30 June 2026.

4
00:00:08,751 --> 00:00:13,127
No journal can be dated on or before that
day, from any

5
00:00:13,127 --> 00:00:17,137
screen, so a month you have reported
cannot change underneath you.

6
00:00:17,137 --> 00:00:21,513
September has ended, so enter 30 September
2026 and select Lock through.

7
00:00:21,513 --> 00:00:22,242
Miftah refuses.

8
00:00:22,242 --> 00:00:25,888
September's rent has not been recognised
yet, and a lock

9
00:00:25,888 --> 00:00:29,170
now would strand that income in a closed
period.

10
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:33,546
The message names the month and how many
periods are still planned.

11
00:00:33,546 --> 00:00:36,098
Select the link to open Month-end
recognition.

12
00:00:36,098 --> 00:00:39,015
Set the date to 30 September and preview.

13
00:00:39,015 --> 00:00:41,932
Nine contract periods for September are
still planned.

14
00:00:41,932 --> 00:00:43,390
Run recognition and confirm.

15
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:45,578
Each period becomes one income journal.

16
00:00:45,578 --> 00:00:49,589
It moves that month's rent from Advance
Rent to Rental Income,

17
00:00:49,589 --> 00:00:53,235
at the contract's day rate for every day
of September.

18
00:00:53,235 --> 00:00:55,788
A run never posts the same period

19
00:00:55,788 --> 00:00:58,340
twice, so it is safe to repeat.

20
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:01,257
When the run finishes, Miftah shows nine
posted,

21
00:01:01,257 --> 00:01:04,174
and the warning at the top is gone.

22
00:01:04,174 --> 00:01:07,820
Back on Year End Closing, lock through 30
September again.

23
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:12,196
This time the lock moves, and the sidebar
shows the new date.

24
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:14,748
September is posted, so nothing is
stranded.

25
00:01:14,748 --> 00:01:16,936
Now read the Fiscal years list.

26
00:01:16,936 --> 00:01:18,759
The year 2025 is Closed.

27
00:01:18,759 --> 00:01:21,311
Palm Ridge's books started on 1 September

28
00:01:21,311 --> 00:01:23,864
2025, so that year held four months.

29
00:01:23,864 --> 00:01:27,510
To open its year-end closing journal, go
to Journal Voucher,

30
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:30,792
set the type to YEC, apply, and open
YEC-25/1.

31
00:01:30,792 --> 00:01:35,167
It empties every income account and every
expense account for the year,

32
00:01:35,167 --> 00:01:39,178
building by building, and puts the net
result into Retained Earnings,

33
00:01:39,178 --> 00:01:43,189
the equity account that carries the profit
the business has kept.

34
00:01:43,189 --> 00:01:46,106
Now open the Trial Balance, enter 31
December

35
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,658
2025 as the date, and select Apply.

36
00:01:48,658 --> 00:01:52,669
Each income and expense account shows
equal debits and credits, so

37
00:01:52,669 --> 00:01:56,680
its balance is zero, and Retained Earnings
holds the year's profit.

38
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:59,962
Select Before closing entries to see the
same day

39
00:01:59,962 --> 00:02:02,879
as the accountant reviewed it before the
close.

40
00:02:02,879 --> 00:02:05,796
Now income shows only its credit for the

41
00:02:05,796 --> 00:02:08,348
year, and the expenses only their debit.

42
00:02:08,348 --> 00:02:12,359
Back on Year End Closing, open the close
preview for 2026.

43
00:02:12,359 --> 00:02:16,005
The year has not ended, so Miftah lists
what still

44
00:02:16,005 --> 00:02:19,651
stands in the way: the year end must be in

45
00:02:19,651 --> 00:02:22,933
the past, the rest of the year's income
must

46
00:02:22,933 --> 00:02:26,215
be recognised, and VAT tax points must be
declared.

47
00:02:26,215 --> 00:02:28,767
Below, the preview shows the net result

48
00:02:28,767 --> 00:02:31,319
each building will carry into Retained
Earnings.

49
00:02:31,319 --> 00:02:34,236
If a closed year must change, the Company

50
00:02:34,236 --> 00:02:36,789
Admin selects Re-open and gives a reason.

51
00:02:36,789 --> 00:02:39,706
Miftah reverses the closing journal and
moves the

52
00:02:39,706 --> 00:02:42,623
lock back to the start of that year.

53
00:02:42,623 --> 00:02:45,540
Post the correction, then close the year
again.

54
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:48,092
The first closing journal stays, marked as

55
00:02:48,092 --> 00:02:50,280
reversed, so the trail is complete.
